  "id": "Compound::DB01131 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Proguanil exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c19, which is involved in multiple enzymatic activities, including arachidonic acid epoxygenation and monooxygenation, as well as steroid hydroxylation. These activities are all mediated by Cyp2d6, suggesting a potential role for Proguanil in modulating the metabolic pathways of arachidonic acid and steroids. The consistent binding and participation relationships across the three paths indicate a plausible mechanism by which Proguanil may influence Cyp2d6 function. The shared involvement of Cyp2c19 in multiple metabolic processes implies that Proguanil could potentially affect the activity of Cyp2d6 through a common intermediate, thereby influencing steroid and arachidonic acid metabolism. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Proguanil and Cyp2d6, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
